    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Corbin Carroll**, who commands an elite score of 84.82 against Griffin Canning. His matchup is the premier opportunity on the board, benefiting from a soft SP_xERA of 4.76 and a favorable batting order position. **Seiya Suzuki** is our secondary force, surging to a 73.90 score by capitalizing on a substantial +16% park factor and an 18% SP Skill advantage against Trevor Rogers. Both **Brice Turang** and **Mickey Moniak** are start-worthy, with **Turang** drawing a +4% efficiency boost due to the slow delivery of Pallante\u2014a critical metric for our aggressive stolen base strategy\u2014and **Moniak** enjoying a +5% wind-out advantage that helps mitigate the platoon disadvantage against Carson Whisenhunt.\n\nOur toughest roster exclusion today is **Jose Caballero**, whose 39.32 score landed just shy of the 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" required for starting eligibility. While **Caballero** offers high-upside speed, the optimizer penalized him heavily for the -16% SP Skill hurdle presented by Rasmussen. Consequently, we are prioritizing the higher floor of **Cole Young**, despite his own middling score of 47.41. We are monitoring **Gabriel Moreno**, **Brice Turang**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Kyle Karros** closely; as these players are currently under \"Lineup Pending\" status, their scores are tied to assumed order placements. Any significant deviation from these projected slots in the official daily lineup could necessitate a recalibration of our efficiency expectations before first pitch.",
